WEBVTT

00:02.960 --> 00:05.670
THE ELUSIVE
SAMURAI

01:25.290 --> 01:29.960
THE ELUSIVE
SAMURAI

01:30.670 --> 01:35.470
FINAL EPISODE

01:35.550 --> 01:39.340
<i>Though I see a future where you live,</i>
<i>it is not guaranteed.</i>

01:42.430 --> 01:45.560
<i>Naturally, if you neglect</i>
<i>the fight for survival, you will die.</i>

01:49.350 --> 01:54.570
<i>But the experience that you'll gain</i>
<i>by going into battle is immeasurable.</i>

01:56.110 --> 01:58.780
<i>I pray for your safe return,</i>
<i>Lord Tokiyuki.</i>

01:59.360 --> 02:01.780
Let the women and children escape first!

02:01.870 --> 02:03.790
If they can escape
through the defensive barriers,

02:03.870 --> 02:05.540
we can hold off
the great enemy army there!

02:05.620 --> 02:07.040
HOSHINA'S ARMY
PROVINCIAL OFFICIAL'S ARMY

02:07.120 --> 02:08.710
Turn around!

02:09.210 --> 02:11.880
We'll defend as one unit
against the enemy from the rear!

02:11.960 --> 02:17.800
Listen, grunts!
The idiots are turning back!

02:17.880 --> 02:20.140
Provincial official's orders!

02:20.220 --> 02:21.800
Kill all the men!

02:21.890 --> 02:25.310
We'll divide the women, children,
and the loot equally!

02:25.390 --> 02:26.810
NANBOKUCHO GAME OF TAG

02:26.890 --> 02:28.560
BURNING DEMON BRIGADE
PROVINCIAL OFFICIAL'S GUARD

02:28.640 --> 02:29.850
HIS FACE LOOKS LIKE THIS

02:29.940 --> 02:30.940
According to Shizuku,

02:31.020 --> 02:34.440
the one named Yonemaru Wada is leading
the provincial official's private force.

02:34.530 --> 02:36.530
A FEW HOURS EARLIER
WITHIN THE HOSHINA PARTY CAMP

02:36.610 --> 02:40.070
If we can just take him down, we'll
weaken the provincial official's army.

02:41.110 --> 02:42.280
Take him down?

02:42.780 --> 02:44.700
You've got it backwards, Kojiro.

02:44.790 --> 02:47.620
First, we'll take advantage of him,
then weaken his army.

02:51.500 --> 02:56.880
Come on! Come on!
Follow me! Climb that mountain!

02:56.960 --> 02:58.630
What?

02:58.720 --> 03:01.180
Weren't we all going to chase down
the Hoshina party together?

03:01.260 --> 03:02.550
You idiots!

03:02.640 --> 03:05.140
We can surround the enemy from behind
if we go over the mountain!

03:05.220 --> 03:07.770
We can annihilate them
with a pincer attack!

03:08.270 --> 03:11.020
Follow me now or I'll kill you, got it?

03:11.100 --> 03:12.900
Yes, sir!

03:12.980 --> 03:15.690
This battle of retreat
will be on flat land.

03:16.480 --> 03:18.440
Tactics like ambushes can't be used,

03:18.530 --> 03:21.320
which puts the outnumbered Hoshina party
at a great disadvantage.

03:21.410 --> 03:25.410
In this case,
we want to divide the enemy's troops.

03:25.950 --> 03:29.250
And one of us has what it takes!

03:30.080 --> 03:32.000
Keep up with Lord Yonemaru!

03:32.080 --> 03:33.460
Keep climbing!

03:33.540 --> 03:35.000
What's happening?

03:35.090 --> 03:37.460
Lord Yonemaru, what is this?

03:37.550 --> 03:38.380
Hey.

03:38.460 --> 03:44.390
-Lord Yonemaru, please direct us!
-Hey… Hey… Hey… Hey?

03:45.050 --> 03:45.890
Hey?

03:45.970 --> 03:46.970
Hey, who am I again?

03:47.060 --> 03:47.890
POP

03:47.970 --> 03:49.640
Who the hell are you?

03:49.730 --> 03:50.560
Hup.

03:50.640 --> 03:54.810
I see. Yesterday, you memorized
how he looks to morph into him.

03:58.940 --> 04:02.610
Mr. Messenger's retainers
aren't too shabby.

04:03.490 --> 04:05.070
I get it.

04:05.160 --> 04:09.660
Kawanakajima's Suwa party are
all highly skilled.

04:11.000 --> 04:13.040
How do you like that, Mr. Messenger?

04:13.750 --> 04:16.130
We're strong when resigned to die,

04:16.210 --> 04:19.000
and we're also strong
when we are willed to live!

04:19.590 --> 04:20.630
Yes.

04:21.630 --> 04:26.010
Even so… Escaping won't be easy.

04:27.010 --> 04:29.720
After the women and children
relocate somewhere safe,

04:29.810 --> 04:32.770
we have to shake off the enemy and escape.

04:33.440 --> 04:37.230
Come to think of it,
where's your vigorous friend?

04:38.980 --> 04:42.320
I've ordered Kojiro
to move of his own accord.

04:42.820 --> 04:46.160
I'm sure he'll be of great help
to you and your men.

04:48.160 --> 04:49.990
<i>I'll perform a hit-and-run.</i>

04:50.080 --> 04:53.830
<i>At my age,</i>
<i>I'm at a disadvantage against adults.</i>

04:54.670 --> 04:57.670
<i>I'll utilize my small stature</i>
<i>to escape to high ground</i>

04:57.750 --> 05:00.550
<i>and seek allies who need my assistance.</i>

05:03.050 --> 05:06.890
<i>I'll deliver an effective blow</i>
<i>then retreat to that high ground.</i>

05:08.180 --> 05:12.600
<i>By repeating this tactic, I've begun</i>
<i>to see the dynamic of the entire battle</i>

05:12.680 --> 05:14.730
<i>and where I should fight next.</i>

05:16.190 --> 05:18.110
<i>I want help from the Hoshina party.</i>

05:18.770 --> 05:20.570
<i>I need four or five men.</i>

05:20.650 --> 05:23.570
Hey, mister! Please come with me!

05:24.070 --> 05:27.360
You, the old man
with focus lines all over your face!

05:28.240 --> 05:29.740
Focus lines all over my face?

05:29.830 --> 05:32.200
Don't make a straight face now.
It's confusing!

05:32.290 --> 05:35.710
You, the geezer with rectangular features
all over, come with me too.

05:35.790 --> 05:38.290
Rectangular features all over?

05:38.380 --> 05:39.880
I guess that's not me then.

05:39.960 --> 05:43.920
Ugh, don't suddenly add round elements!
Now I can't compare you to anything!

05:44.010 --> 05:44.920
What about me?

05:45.010 --> 05:46.680
Compare me to something!

05:46.760 --> 05:49.090
I don't know! You're some kind of monster!

05:49.180 --> 05:50.300
Just come with me!

05:50.390 --> 05:51.970
The enemy is moving along the riverbank

05:52.060 --> 05:54.560
aiming for the women
and children behind us.

05:54.640 --> 05:57.440
Let's band together
and invade them from the side!

06:03.780 --> 06:05.690
Not a damn chance!

06:05.780 --> 06:07.320
Nice work, baldy!

06:07.400 --> 06:09.320
I'm not bald! Take a good look!

06:09.410 --> 06:11.660
Hair grows on the back of my head,
but I shave it off!

06:11.740 --> 06:14.040
You guys are annoying!

06:14.700 --> 06:18.460
<i>Actually, it's my fault</i>
<i>for not remembering my allies' names.</i>

06:18.540 --> 06:21.670
<i>From now on, I'll make</i>
<i>a round of hellos during mealtime.</i>

06:23.500 --> 06:24.670
Fubuki!

06:25.550 --> 06:27.170
Why are you here?

06:27.260 --> 06:29.430
Your waiting post is further that way.

06:33.140 --> 06:34.430
Fubuki!

06:37.140 --> 06:39.560
Fubuki! Get a hold of yourself!

06:39.650 --> 06:41.400
Are you all right? Hey!

06:43.860 --> 06:46.940
I'm so hungry. I can't move.

06:47.030 --> 06:48.990
You're a dumb flake, aren't you?

06:49.070 --> 06:52.320
You sure do need a lot of calories
in exchange for being smart!

06:52.410 --> 06:54.240
Here, take this fresh manju.

06:54.330 --> 06:56.410
All right, I'm recharged and ready to go!

06:56.500 --> 06:58.750
Hurry up and go back to your waiting post.

06:59.290 --> 07:03.790
Please… Isn't your strategy supposed to be
the cornerstone of the Elusive Warriors?

07:04.550 --> 07:05.880
I'm not special.

07:05.960 --> 07:08.130
Anyone can strategize if you just learn.

07:09.420 --> 07:12.720
You run madly around the battlefield,
fighting selflessly,

07:12.800 --> 07:15.600
initiating conversations
and taking care of allies.

07:16.270 --> 07:19.140
It's a general like that who can become
the cornerstone of a party.

07:19.230 --> 07:23.310
Kojiro, you are a solid adjutant general
of the Elusive Warriors.

07:32.070 --> 07:36.490
Being complimented by someone overflowing
with talent only comes across as sarcasm.

07:42.120 --> 07:44.380
Old man with both rectangular
and circular features

07:44.460 --> 07:45.960
and the other guy that's mostly bald

07:46.040 --> 07:48.710
that shaves the little hair
that is growing on the back of his head!

07:49.800 --> 07:50.970
Hey.

07:51.800 --> 07:55.390
You destroyed my independent unit.

07:56.100 --> 07:57.970
You'll meet your end for this.

08:04.480 --> 08:07.520
You're an apprentice
at Suwa Grand Shrine, huh?

08:07.610 --> 08:11.320
Not that it's somethin'
to write home about.

08:11.400 --> 08:13.070
Shut up, pig.

08:13.570 --> 08:17.370
I'll scatter your smelly fat
around Chikuma River.

08:18.660 --> 08:20.200
-Let the best man win!
-Let the best man win!

08:24.170 --> 08:26.590
<i>The top speed for</i>
<i>the fastest native Japanese horses</i>

08:26.670 --> 08:28.380
<i>is about 40 kilometers per hour,</i>

08:28.460 --> 08:32.720
<i>which is roughly the same speed as</i>
<i>the fastest punch of a professional boxer.</i>

08:33.630 --> 08:37.930
<i>This means that just by bracing one's</i>
<i>curved sword and charging on a horse,</i>

08:38.430 --> 08:40.220
<i>a blade is bound to come flying</i>
<i>at the opponent</i>

08:40.310 --> 08:42.230
<i>at the speed of the world's fastest jab.</i>

08:52.440 --> 08:54.360
<i>You're kidding…</i>

08:55.700 --> 08:56.870
Whoa.

08:58.830 --> 09:00.620
What happened, chump?

09:00.700 --> 09:04.160
You talk big,
but are you as puny as you look?

09:04.250 --> 09:05.420
Ha!

09:07.710 --> 09:09.090
<i>We have a difference in strength,</i>

09:09.170 --> 09:11.260
-<i>weight…</i>
-Come on, come on!

09:11.340 --> 09:13.420
-<i>…and relative speed.</i>
-Come at me! Come on!

09:13.510 --> 09:14.420
Come on!

09:14.510 --> 09:16.260
Take this!

09:18.600 --> 09:20.810
<i>I can't even block</i>
<i>his attacks effectively.</i>

09:21.390 --> 09:22.310
Kojiro!

09:22.390 --> 09:23.600
Get back!

09:23.680 --> 09:26.060
You're no physical match on horseback!

09:26.140 --> 09:27.810
Just run!

09:33.280 --> 09:36.240
<i>If I pull out,</i>
<i>it's over for those old geezers.</i>

09:36.320 --> 09:39.740
<i>Yonemaru will remain as</i>
<i>the only one on horseback.</i>

09:43.250 --> 09:45.830
<i>The infantry are</i>
<i>at a complete disadvantage</i>

09:45.910 --> 09:49.250
<i>compared to the cavalry</i>
<i>in terms of speed and strength.</i>

09:49.330 --> 09:51.670
<i>That's why he targeted</i>
<i>the two cavalrymen first.</i>

09:52.300 --> 09:56.630
<i>If I give up now,</i>
<i>that pig will begin his rampage!</i>

10:07.270 --> 10:10.440
He weakens with every attack.

10:11.270 --> 10:15.440
He doesn't have the strength
to block my next strike.

10:16.860 --> 10:18.610
Hey! Kojiro!

10:19.320 --> 10:20.700
Don't worry about me!

10:20.780 --> 10:23.080
Finish the remaining enemy!

10:26.660 --> 10:30.000
Why does everyone know my name anyways?

10:30.790 --> 10:35.460
Oh, that's because Mr. Messenger
kept calling your name yesterday.

10:36.550 --> 10:39.260
<i>Kojiro! Nice, Kojiro!</i>

10:39.340 --> 10:41.350
<i>Don't you dare die!</i>

10:41.430 --> 10:44.140
<i>Look, that's my retainer Kojiro!</i>

10:44.930 --> 10:48.190
<i>That's my friend Kojiro</i>
<i>killing it out there!</i>

10:49.650 --> 10:51.190
So embarrassing…

10:53.900 --> 10:54.900
<i>But…</i>

10:55.440 --> 10:56.940
<i>Kojiro!</i>

11:02.820 --> 11:04.120
Kojiro!

11:04.700 --> 11:07.000
<i>I have to get in at least one blow</i>

11:07.790 --> 11:11.920
<i>so that I don't embarrass my lord!</i>

11:20.680 --> 11:21.680
<i>No way.</i>

11:22.470 --> 11:25.600
<i>How did someone so large dodge that?</i>

11:26.180 --> 11:28.100
Damn it… Little bastard!

11:28.640 --> 11:31.900
You think you're a real warrior?

11:31.980 --> 11:34.190
You'll pay for this!

11:36.230 --> 11:39.860
<i>A general who can lead an army</i>
<i>sure is something else…</i>

11:40.450 --> 11:44.370
<i>The spirit of a general</i>
<i>is to be boisterous, huh.</i>

11:45.450 --> 11:47.870
<i>I guess I'll try it next time.</i>

11:48.700 --> 11:53.420
<i>But, damn… My strength… is gone…</i>

12:07.260 --> 12:08.560
Oy, kid.

12:16.020 --> 12:17.360
Don't give out now.

12:17.980 --> 12:20.650
I can't let you die so easily.

12:20.740 --> 12:23.280
First I'll rip your arms off one by one…

12:26.160 --> 12:29.040
You let your guard down
and stopped your horse, didn't you?

12:29.750 --> 12:32.790
You've got nobody to help you now!

12:34.290 --> 12:35.460
Get him, Kojiro!

12:36.170 --> 12:38.300
He's your kill!

12:39.090 --> 12:39.960
<i>Oh, man…</i>

12:41.260 --> 12:42.340
<i>It's fun!</i>

12:43.220 --> 12:47.010
<i>Fighting as a unit is fun!</i>

12:48.350 --> 12:50.100
I am Kojiro of the Elusive Warriors!

12:50.180 --> 12:52.480
I'll take your head and your power!

12:53.480 --> 12:55.230
Take this!

12:59.070 --> 13:01.030
PROVINCIAL OFFICIAL'S MAIN ARMY

13:01.110 --> 13:03.200
Why are you all just standing there?

13:03.280 --> 13:05.740
I can't see through this damn fog!

13:05.820 --> 13:08.740
The enemy's rear guard
is fighting with all their might.

13:08.830 --> 13:10.540
They're stuck in a back-and-forth.

13:10.620 --> 13:13.710
Well, we'll be able to crush them
with our numbers,

13:13.790 --> 13:16.830
though the women and children
will get away at this rate.

13:16.920 --> 13:19.670
What? Chase after them, Ichikawa!

13:19.750 --> 13:23.840
I'll carefully pick my favorite women
to be a part of my paradise!

13:23.920 --> 13:24.760
WOMEN

13:24.840 --> 13:28.350
But if we go, you will be left with no…

13:28.930 --> 13:32.100
There's no need for guards
when the enemy are running away!

13:32.180 --> 13:34.940
Do you not understand military strategy,
you country bumpkin?

13:35.020 --> 13:35.940
OFFICIAL

13:36.020 --> 13:37.940
Is your own life so precious?

13:38.020 --> 13:40.940
If you're a soldier,
go fight with your life on the line!

13:41.020 --> 13:42.530
Tsk.

13:42.610 --> 13:44.860
Great…

13:51.240 --> 13:52.660
Lord Hoshina!

13:52.740 --> 13:55.410
All the women and children
escaped to the safe zone!

13:55.500 --> 13:56.460
Good!

13:56.540 --> 13:58.920
Ring the bell
to signal the army's retreat!

13:59.000 --> 14:01.710
Only the rear guard should stay
to distract the enemy!

14:02.920 --> 14:05.090
Mr. Messenger! You've done enough.

14:05.170 --> 14:06.340
Run!

14:07.510 --> 14:09.300
I cannot, Mr. Hoshina.

14:10.010 --> 14:13.770
I must take responsibility for
instructing you and your men to escape.

14:15.180 --> 14:16.770
It's not right that I come this far

14:16.850 --> 14:19.560
and be the only one who does not taste
the fear of being chased…

14:19.650 --> 14:20.980
Wow…

14:21.060 --> 14:24.230
Mr. Messenger, you care about us so much…

14:24.320 --> 14:25.610
<i>It would be a waste!</i>

14:25.690 --> 14:27.820
Withdraw! Withdraw!

14:27.910 --> 14:30.740
Oy! It's the chime to withdraw. Run!

14:32.580 --> 14:33.580
Okay.

14:33.660 --> 14:35.200
STAB STAB STAB

14:36.250 --> 14:38.540
Hoshina's army has begun to withdraw!

14:38.620 --> 14:40.380
Slice them from behind!

14:41.790 --> 14:44.170
<i>Zigzagging and firing backwards?</i>

14:44.760 --> 14:47.590
<i>I can't move forward easily</i>
<i>with horses and arrows in the way.</i>

14:48.180 --> 14:49.590
<i>That damn brat!</i>

14:50.260 --> 14:53.100
<i>Even though we're almost winning…</i>

14:53.180 --> 14:56.680
Sorry, but I'm not dying
from a fatal shot to my vitals.

14:58.350 --> 15:01.690
<i>Once the enemy begins to think about</i>
<i>the rewards for winning the war,</i>

15:02.190 --> 15:05.110
<i>they will no longer risk their lives</i>
<i>at the front lines.</i>

15:06.280 --> 15:09.110
<i>Furthermore, as for the lord retreating</i>
<i>as the helm of the rear guard,</i>

15:09.200 --> 15:11.320
<i>the most perilous position…</i>

15:11.410 --> 15:13.910
Brilliant! Mr. Messenger.

15:16.910 --> 15:18.290
Mr. Messenger!

15:18.370 --> 15:21.920
<i>…you will earn immense trust</i>
<i>from their allies.</i>

15:23.000 --> 15:26.590
<i>Meanwhile, I'll finish the war</i>
<i>with my own blade!</i>

15:26.670 --> 15:27.800
<i>Crap!</i>

15:27.880 --> 15:29.880
<i>He's aiming for the provincial official!</i>

15:30.380 --> 15:33.010
<i>The blame will fall on me.</i>
<i>They'll kill me!</i>

15:33.640 --> 15:35.810
My provincial official!
Incoming from the right!

15:36.390 --> 15:37.640
What?

15:37.720 --> 15:41.140
That incapable Ichikawa
is screaming something.

15:41.230 --> 15:44.230
He's still chickening out
after coming this far?

15:44.310 --> 15:47.570
<i>Choosing the moment we'd leave</i>
<i>the provincial official's guard!</i>

15:47.650 --> 15:49.530
<i>The morning mist hiding his location!</i>

15:49.610 --> 15:52.490
<i>The army's footsteps masking his approach!</i>

15:52.570 --> 15:55.160
<i>Did he calculate all of this?</i>

15:56.330 --> 15:58.580
Don't come back, coward!

15:58.660 --> 16:02.000
If you don't obey my tactics…

16:02.750 --> 16:04.080
Huh?

16:10.420 --> 16:12.380
My provincial official! Are you all right?

16:12.470 --> 16:14.390
He cut me!

16:14.470 --> 16:16.010
He cut me!

16:16.100 --> 16:22.900
He tried to kill me, the provincial
official appointed by the Emperor!

16:23.480 --> 16:25.230
<i>Killing him would be a poor plan.</i>

16:25.310 --> 16:28.400
<i>An incompetent enemy general</i>
<i>is more useful alive.</i>

16:28.980 --> 16:30.400
My provincial official!

16:30.490 --> 16:32.320
Beyond the river!

16:32.400 --> 16:34.200
There are large shadows of flags!

16:34.280 --> 16:36.830
We don't have allies there!

16:38.990 --> 16:41.660
Another troop coming for my head!

16:42.460 --> 16:43.540
Calm down.

16:43.620 --> 16:45.790
There's no sound of soldiers moving.

16:45.880 --> 16:47.670
They may have just raised flags
to trick us.

16:47.750 --> 16:49.340
You idiot!

16:49.420 --> 16:51.380
It looks like they're about to charge!

16:51.470 --> 16:53.630
Hurry, command Yonemaru's army back here!

16:53.720 --> 16:56.430
Sound the drums to signal withdrawal!

16:59.520 --> 17:01.180
<i>Damn provincial official!</i>

17:01.270 --> 17:05.230
Setaro! Take Yonemaru's place
and lead our soldiers to the front lines!

17:05.310 --> 17:06.150
Sir!

17:06.230 --> 17:07.060
HOSHINA TERRITORY

17:07.150 --> 17:09.020
Once you drive Hoshina beyond his barrier,

17:09.110 --> 17:11.940
build another one of our own
to secure the territory.

17:12.030 --> 17:13.400
PROVINCIAL OFFICIAL'S TERRITORY

17:14.740 --> 17:18.830
<i>Our easy victory is ruined because of him!</i>

17:18.910 --> 17:22.160
<i>This provincial official is</i>
<i>a burden on us.</i>

17:22.250 --> 17:23.250
Tsk.

17:24.460 --> 17:27.040
Oh! The enemy is withdrawing!

17:28.040 --> 17:30.090
<i>Fubuki's strategy was a success!</i>

17:31.840 --> 17:35.220
They'll come to attack us once
they realize the standards are decoys.

17:35.300 --> 17:37.890
Let's run past the barrier while we can!

17:37.970 --> 17:39.220
All right!

17:52.440 --> 17:53.440
My lord!

17:53.530 --> 17:55.320
Kojiro!

17:55.400 --> 17:57.700
-You took quite a while.
-Huh?

17:58.570 --> 18:00.370
You got the kill, right?

18:00.450 --> 18:01.290
Fubuki!

18:01.370 --> 18:02.740
It was amazing.

18:02.830 --> 18:04.830
He took down Yonemaru.

18:04.910 --> 18:06.000
Well done!

18:06.080 --> 18:07.620
Where is his head for proof?

18:11.550 --> 18:13.760
I left him with it.

18:13.840 --> 18:16.800
He taught me a lot.

18:17.930 --> 18:22.390
Even if I did have his head,
you can't give me a reward, right?

18:22.470 --> 18:24.810
Since you just lost half your territory.

18:24.890 --> 18:26.020
Shut up.

18:26.100 --> 18:27.270
It's true.

18:28.350 --> 18:29.190
Anyhow…

18:30.270 --> 18:34.360
Losing has never felt so good.

18:35.150 --> 18:36.070
Lord Hoshina!

18:36.150 --> 18:37.200
Mr. Messenger!

18:37.780 --> 18:39.700
Lord Hoshina, you're safe!

18:39.780 --> 18:41.120
Mr. Messenger!

18:41.200 --> 18:43.490
Lord Hoshina did it again!

18:43.580 --> 18:47.960
We lost our territory,
but it's as if we won.

18:49.000 --> 18:54.250
We get to see these smiles
because we escaped and survived.

18:57.010 --> 19:00.010
<i>Afterwards, Hoshina ruled</i>
<i>a small area in northern Shinano,</i>

19:00.090 --> 19:03.680
<i>and he was driven out to the south.</i>

19:05.100 --> 19:08.100
<i>Lords often change</i>
<i>as time passes. However…</i>

19:08.980 --> 19:09.980
Boing.

19:12.020 --> 19:14.650
<i>By skillfully overcoming crises</i>
<i>time and time again,</i>

19:14.730 --> 19:16.400
-<i>the Hoshina party became…</i>
-Good work!

19:16.490 --> 19:18.740
<i>…a resilient feudal lord lineage</i>
<i>that endured until the Meiji era.</i>

19:19.360 --> 19:22.450
<i>And more importantly for Tokiyuki,</i>

19:22.530 --> 19:27.000
<i>they would become a crucial military force</i>
<i>in the nearing uprising.</i>

19:28.080 --> 19:31.670
Please let Myojin know that we,
the Hoshina party,

19:31.750 --> 19:35.750
were saved by Mr. Messenger
and his retainers.

19:35.840 --> 19:38.590
Let him know that we'll treasure
the precious life we were given

19:38.670 --> 19:44.260
whether by losing or escaping, and we
shall dedicate our lives to serve Myojin.

19:45.430 --> 19:46.600
Yes.

19:46.680 --> 19:47.680
GRUMBLE

19:48.770 --> 19:52.310
Mr. Messenger,
please stop by our territory.

19:52.900 --> 19:55.570
We don't have much,
but we want to repay you.

19:56.690 --> 19:58.070
Dinner!

20:00.700 --> 20:05.370
You know, brat,
it's rude to refuse a gift.

20:06.410 --> 20:09.080
I want to return quickly
to let them know we're safe.

20:09.160 --> 20:10.750
Everyone's probably worried.

20:11.420 --> 20:13.630
You can stay here by yourself, you know.

20:13.710 --> 20:16.800
The Young Lord only needs us as guards.

20:16.880 --> 20:20.420
I was given a gift, as well, so…

20:20.510 --> 20:23.260
Tsk. Goody Two-shoes.

20:23.340 --> 20:24.470
Thank you.

20:24.550 --> 20:27.220
Kojiro, Fubuki, Genba.

20:28.270 --> 20:31.270
Oh, I don't need
a thank-you dinner or anything…

20:38.440 --> 20:39.440
Okay!

20:39.530 --> 20:42.610
My lord, you performed brilliantly.

20:42.700 --> 20:46.660
You owe me a lot of money for this war.

20:56.420 --> 20:58.630
Oh, I fell asleep.

20:59.920 --> 21:01.470
Father?

21:02.090 --> 21:03.630
The war is over.

21:04.380 --> 21:07.350
Lord Tokiyuki will return soon.

21:10.970 --> 21:13.230
I'm so glad the Young Lord is safe!

21:13.310 --> 21:14.850
Let's celebrate when he returns.

21:14.940 --> 21:17.560
Yes! Let's make a lot of delicious food!

21:17.650 --> 21:19.690
We have to prepare before he returns.

21:19.780 --> 21:21.650
Let's cook some meat to give him energy.

21:21.740 --> 21:24.450
Don't blow it into too many pieces.

21:25.110 --> 21:27.490
Let's continue to build alliances!

21:27.570 --> 21:29.120
We'll turn samurai who want to die

21:29.200 --> 21:31.500
into samurai who want to live
and fight with us!

21:32.120 --> 21:33.120
Huh?

21:41.670 --> 21:44.630
What happened? Is there an enemy?
What's gotten into you?

21:44.720 --> 21:45.930
There's a rainbow.

21:46.010 --> 21:47.470
Yes, I see it too.

21:47.550 --> 21:49.510
Hey, don't spray it on me.

22:04.740 --> 22:06.740
THE ELUSIVE SAMURAI

23:38.960 --> 23:39.830
<i>Let's go!</i>
